.TH LIBMPQ__BLOCK_SIZE_UNPACKED 3 2026-08-12 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__block_size_unpacked \- return the unpacked size of one block.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__block_size_unpacked("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s  *" "mpq_archive",
.BI "        uint32_t        " "file_number",
.BI "        uint32_t        " "block_number",
.BI "        libmpq__off_t *" "unpacked_size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Call \fBlibmpq__block_size_unpacked\fP() to get the unpacked size of one block.
.LP
The first argument is an archive handle opened by
\fBlibmpq__archive_open\fP(). The \fIfile_number\fP and \fIblock_number\fP
arguments select the block. The function stores its unpacked size in
\fIunpacked_size\fP. The block offset table must be open with
\fBlibmpq__block_open_offset\fP().
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, a zero is returned and on error one of the following constants.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST
The file or block does not exist in the archive.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_OPEN
The block offset table is not open.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_size_unpacked (3),
.BR libmpq__file_size_unpacked (3)
